[
    {
        "content": "<p>This is a follow up to a prior thread on adding a word RAM model to CSLib. The proposed design lives as a <a href=\"https://github.com/Shreyas4991/Algolean/pull/92\">PR in my library</a>. </p>\n<div class=\"spoiler-block\"><div class=\"spoiler-header\">\n<p>design overview</p>\n</div><div class=\"spoiler-content\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<ol>\n<li>It defines a query type for the word RAM model. This is still familiar to those who know my query-combinator proposal</li>\n<li>But this time, the queries don't take or return lean values. They always return <code>()</code> and take as inputs, registers. </li>\n<li>Valid <code>Prog</code>s don't take the inputs or input-size as a parameter. Those are loaded into the memory and registers. </li>\n<li>There's a separate Problems folder which defines problems and valid input encodings (this turned out to be very important to ensure our <code>Prog</code>s stay uniform over input size). </li>\n<li>The actual memory, registers, and flags of the WordRAM model are now hidden behind the Model (which is now monadic as opposed both <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/cslib/pull/685\">cslib#685</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/cslib/pull/401\">cslib#401</a>). I think the generalization to a state monad based model is a general solution to encode ADTs to data structures as well.</li>\n<li>Because we don't have access to any data from the algorithm, we can't re-use lean's <code>if-then-else</code> and <code>while</code> loops. So there are now constructors for those.</li>\n<li>Because we don't have access to lean's termination checking machinery for these custom loops, we introduce a fuelled execution function and our proofs of correctness and complexity rely on there existing a suitably large fuel to run an algorithm correctly </li>\n</ol>\n<p>Point 6 means we essentially have a fully deeply embedded DSL, but is still inside a Free monad. This is to keep the wordRAM in my query-combinator web of reductions. But now the wordRAM model is cheat-proof with no room for pure operations. </p>\n</div></div>\n<p>Why did I bother implementing this when I have been pitching lightweight monadic verification? </p>\n<div class=\"spoiler-block\"><div class=\"spoiler-header\">\n<p>answers</p>\n</div><div class=\"spoiler-content\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<ol start=\"0\">\n<li>These are technically still programs in the query combinator framework</li>\n<li>As I mentioned before, the moral justification for a lightweight approach with explicit query models is that we can reduce some of them through a sequence of reductions to a basic model. This model is such a basic model.</li>\n<li>Being able to fit lightweight verification and implementation-based heavy-weight algorithms spec into the same framework seems interesting.</li>\n<li>I am still not dealing with identifiers and substitutions where I don't need to, see the register names in the example below.</li>\n</ol>\n</div></div>\n<p>CC : <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"121542\">@Alexandre Rademaker</span> <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"929508\">@Fabrizio Montesi</span> <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"816123\">@user202729</span> and <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"619540\">@Johannes Tantow</span>  <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"948935\">@Christian Reitwiessner</span> (everybody who has shown interest in this topic). </p>\n<p>There's still a lot of polishing and golfing to do. I'll just post the linear search example below:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"sd\">/-- Current address, and the result register on success. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">abbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">index</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Register</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- Search key supplied by the initial machine state. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">abbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">key</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Register</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- Scratch register for the loaded input word. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">abbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">value</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Register</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- Register holding the constant one. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">abbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">one</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Register</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- Inclusive last input address, loaded from the size header. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">abbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">last</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Register</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- Inspect one cell, stopping at the first match or the inclusive last address. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">body</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Prog</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">WordRAM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">WordRAM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">value</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←ᵣ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mem</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">index</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">ifₚ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">value</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=ᵣ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">key</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">reset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ult</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">else</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">ifₚ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">index</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;ᵣ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">last</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">index</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←ᵣ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">index</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">one</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">else</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">nop</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- Read the size header and initialize the search at address one. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">setup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Prog</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">WordRAM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">WordRAM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">reset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">eq</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">index</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←ᵣ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">imm</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">last</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←ᵣ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mem</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">index</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">cmp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ult</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">index</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">last</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">one</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←ᵣ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">imm</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">index</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←ᵣ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">imm</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- Convert a found memory address to a zero-based array index. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">finish</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Prog</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">WordRAM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">WordRAM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">ifₚ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">flag</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">eq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">index</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←ᵣ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">index</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">one</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">else</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">nop</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">...</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">linearSearch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Prog</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">WordRAM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">WordRAM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">LinearSearch</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">setup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">whileₚ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ult</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">LinearSearch</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">body</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">LinearSearch</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">finish</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 624663576,
        "sender_full_name": "Shreyas Srinivas",
        "timestamp": 1789568585
    },
    {
        "content": "<blockquote>\n<p>As I mentioned before, the moral justification for a lightweight approach with explicit query models is that we can reduce some of them through a sequence of reductions to a basic model. This model is such a basic model.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Maybe I'm missing something, but don't these less basic models usually allow binds/pure lean computation? I don't see how a reduction to this model would work in that case.</p>",
        "id": 624766110,
        "sender_full_name": "Sebastian Zimmer",
        "timestamp": 1789590813
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don’t claim that it helps in every case. But I’m also not trying to formalise every algorithm to this implementable detail.</p>",
        "id": 624766328,
        "sender_full_name": "Shreyas Srinivas",
        "timestamp": 1789590885
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I am sharply focused on the needs of algorithms theory and for this, lightweight formalisation is the right abstraction</p>",
        "id": 624766449,
        "sender_full_name": "Shreyas Srinivas",
        "timestamp": 1789590926
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>For the vast majority this theory we even want to use pure operations. The reduction is handy when we wish to formalize some of these algorithms and get implementations out of them. </p>\n<p>case in point: you can reduce the ADTs for data structures and for the special case where they store wordRAM words, reduce them to this word RAM. And then depending on the extent of “pure” code you use in higher level models, you can get some runnable word ram level code.</p>",
        "id": 624766908,
        "sender_full_name": "Shreyas Srinivas",
        "timestamp": 1789591098
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Of course if you wish to directly program in this model, or write a more sophisticated language on top of this assembly level code, that option remains open. You might for example consider a higher level language with scoped variables recursion and what not. A mini C if you will.</p>",
        "id": 624767031,
        "sender_full_name": "Shreyas Srinivas",
        "timestamp": 1789591150
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Could you show a desugared version of your <code>body</code> above?</p>",
        "id": 624974662,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1789651782
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Here:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ForReview</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WordRAM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- The same search step as `body`, using ordinary `do` notation and explicit operations. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bodyExplicit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Prog</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">WordRAM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">load</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">value</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">index</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">cmp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">eq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">value</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">key</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">branch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">eq</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">clearFlag</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ult</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">pure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">())</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">cmp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ult</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">index</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">last</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">branch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ult</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"n\">binop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">add</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">index</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">index</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">one</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"n\">WordRAM</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">nop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"o\">)))</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- The explicit version is definitionally equal to the version written with notation. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bodyExplicit_eq_body</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bodyExplicit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">body</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ForReview</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 624983479,
        "sender_full_name": "Shreyas Srinivas",
        "timestamp": 1789653593
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>the <code>do [WordRAM w k]</code> syntax adds the <code>WordRAM w k</code>annotation for every line. Basically otherwise, lean doesn't infer <code>w</code></p>",
        "id": 624984884,
        "sender_full_name": "Shreyas Srinivas",
        "timestamp": 1789653835
    }
]